        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_133h",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_133h\n\ntest_133h ran one do_facet round trip per proc parameter to\ncheck that each ends with a newline. Each facet has 700 or\nmore such parameters, so the test is dominated by process\nand ssh startup rather than by reading the parameters. It\naverages 14.5 minutes in CI.\n\nRun the loop over the parameters once per facet on the\nremote node and report only the names that fail, then dump\nand fail on those as before. The same parameters are\nchecked with the same awk test, and a parameter without a\ntrailing newline is still reported.\n\nOn a local VM cluster (client, MDS, OSS with 4 OSTs; 709,\n749 and 672 parameters on the client, mds1 and ost1) the\ntest went from 1462 seconds to 25 and 28 seconds.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=133h\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ibf77b841b4d712d78d5a389cf73da62faa588fe2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
